{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Outside shall the sword bereave.</b> Outside the city the sword of armies shall bereave them." "<b>And from the chambers — terror.</b> When he flees and escapes, the chambers of his heart pound upon him from terror, and he dies while walking about in it (Sifrei). Another interpretation: <b>And from the chambers — terror</b> — in the house there shall be the terror of plague, as it is said (Jeremiah 9) ״כִּי עָלָה מָוֶת בְּחַלּוֹנֵינוּ״, and so Onkelos renders. Another interpretation: <b>Outside shall the sword bereave</b> — for what they did in the streets, as it is said ״וּמִסְפַּר חוּצוֹת יְרוּשָׁלַיִם שַׂמְתֶּם מִזְבְּחוֹת לַבֹּשֶׁת״ (ibid. 11); <b>and from the chambers — terror</b>, for what they did in the inner chambers, as it is said ״אֲשֶׁר זִקְנֵי בֵית יִשְׂרָאֵל עוֹשִׂים בַחֹשֶׁךְ אִישׁ בְּחַדְרֵי מַשְׂכִּיתוֹ״ (Ezekiel 8)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:23.242391822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}